1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,140
PRESENTER: Last summer, my
family and I visited Russia.

2
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:05,500
Even though none of
us could read Russian,

3
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:08,180
we did not have any trouble
in figuring our way out,

4
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:11,630
all thanks to Google's real time
translation of Russian boards

5
00:00:11,630 --> 00:00:12,750
into English.

6
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:16,560
This is just one of the several
applications of neural networks.

7
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:20,030
Neural networks form the base
of deep learning, a subfield

8
00:00:20,030 --> 00:00:22,190
of machine learning,
where the algorithms are

9
00:00:22,190 --> 00:00:24,900
inspired by the structure
of the human brain.

10
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:27,860
Neural networks take in
data, train themselves

11
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:30,170
to recognize the
patterns in this data,

12
00:00:30,170 --> 00:00:34,170
and then predict the outputs
for a new set of similar data.

13
00:00:34,170 --> 00:00:36,530
Let's understand
how this is done.

14
00:00:36,530 --> 00:00:38,780
Let's construct a
neural network that

15
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:42,390
differentiates between a
square, circle, and triangle.

16
00:00:42,390 --> 00:00:45,480
Neural networks are made
up of layers of neurons.

17
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:49,590
These neurons are the core
processing units of the network.

18
00:00:49,590 --> 00:00:53,130
First, we have the input layer,
which receives the input.

19
00:00:53,130 --> 00:00:56,200
The output layer predicts
our final output.

20
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:58,580
In between, exist
the hidden layers

21
00:00:58,580 --> 00:01:01,770
which perform most of
the computations required

22
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:02,950
by our network.

23
00:01:02,950 --> 00:01:04,900
Here's an image of a circle.

24
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:08,520
This image is composed
of 28 by 28 pixels,

25
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:11,740
which make up for 784 pixels.

26
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:16,630
Each pixel is fed as input to
each neuron of the first layer.

27
00:01:16,630 --> 00:01:18,540
Neurons of one
layer are connected

28
00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:21,520
to neurons of the next
layer through channels.

29
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:24,720
Each of these channels is
assigned a numerical value

30
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:25,930
known as weight.

31
00:01:25,930 --> 00:01:29,310
The inputs are multiplied to
the corresponding weights,

32
00:01:29,310 --> 00:01:32,430
and their sum is sent
as input to the neurons

33
00:01:32,430 --> 00:01:33,880
in the hidden layer.

34
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:36,300
Each of these
neurons is associated

35
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:39,390
with a numerical value
called the bias, which

36
00:01:39,390 --> 00:01:41,500
is then added to the input sum.

37
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:44,730
This value is then passed
through a threshold function

38
00:01:44,730 --> 00:01:47,020
called the activation function.

39
00:01:47,020 --> 00:01:49,320
The result of the
activation function

40
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:52,770
determines if the particular
neuron will get activated

41
00:01:52,770 --> 00:01:53,780
or not.

42
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:56,220
An activated neuron
transmits data

43
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:59,790
to the neurons of the next
layer over the channels.

44
00:01:59,790 --> 00:02:03,550
In this manner, the data is
propagated through the network.

45
00:02:03,550 --> 00:02:06,430
This is called
forward propagation.

46
00:02:06,430 --> 00:02:09,630
In the output layer, the
neuron with the highest value

47
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:11,860
fires and determines the output.

48
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:14,530
The values are
basically a probability.

49
00:02:14,530 --> 00:02:18,060
For example, here, our
neuron associated with square

50
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:20,170
has the highest probability.

51
00:02:20,170 --> 00:02:24,070
Hence, that's the output
predicted by the neural network.

52
00:02:24,070 --> 00:02:26,700
Of course, just by
a look at it, we

53
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:29,310
know our neural network has
made a wrong prediction,

54
00:02:29,310 --> 00:02:32,440
but how does the
network figure this out?

55
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:35,500
Note that our network
is yet to be trained.

56
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:38,850
During this training process,
along with the input,

57
00:02:38,850 --> 00:02:41,890
our network also has
the output fed to it.

58
00:02:41,890 --> 00:02:45,390
The predicted output is compared
against the actual output

59
00:02:45,390 --> 00:02:47,560
to realize the
error in prediction.

60
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:50,640
The magnitude of the error
indicates how wrong we are,

61
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:53,430
and the sign suggests if
our predicted values are

62
00:02:53,430 --> 00:02:55,650
higher or lower than expected.

63
00:02:55,650 --> 00:02:57,870
The arrows here
give an indication

64
00:02:57,870 --> 00:03:01,740
of the direction and magnitude
of change to reduce the error.

65
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:04,890
This information is then
transferred backward

66
00:03:04,890 --> 00:03:06,070
through our network.

67
00:03:06,070 --> 00:03:08,590
This is known as
back propagation.

68
00:03:08,590 --> 00:03:13,390
Now, based on this information,
the weights are adjusted.

69
00:03:13,390 --> 00:03:16,740
This cycle of forward
propagation and back propagation

70
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:20,320
is iteratively performed
with multiple inputs.

71
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:22,770
This process continues
until our weights

72
00:03:22,770 --> 00:03:25,740
are assigned, such that the
network can predict the shapes

73
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:28,120
correctly in most of the cases.

74
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:31,140
This brings our training
process to an end.

75
00:03:31,140 --> 00:03:34,450
You might wonder, how long
this training process takes.

76
00:03:34,450 --> 00:03:38,070
Honestly, neural networks
may take hours or even months

77
00:03:38,070 --> 00:03:41,370
to train, but time is
a reasonable trade-off

78
00:03:41,370 --> 00:03:43,260
when compared to its scope.

79
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:47,140
Let us look at some of the prime
applications of neural networks.

80
00:03:47,140 --> 00:03:49,980
Facial recognition--
cameras on smartphones

81
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:52,500
these days can estimate
the age of the person

82
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:54,370
based on their facial features.

83
00:03:54,370 --> 00:03:56,500
This is neural networks at play.

84
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:59,370
First differentiating the
face from the background,

85
00:03:59,370 --> 00:04:02,250
and then correlating the
lines and spots on your face

86
00:04:02,250 --> 00:04:03,820
to a possible age.

87
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:05,940
Forecasting--
neural networks are

88
00:04:05,940 --> 00:04:07,530
trained to understand
the patterns

89
00:04:07,530 --> 00:04:09,780
and detect the
possibility of rainfall,

90
00:04:09,780 --> 00:04:13,450
or a rise in stock prices
with high accuracy.

91
00:04:13,450 --> 00:04:15,960
Music composition--
neural networks

92
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:19,019
can even learn patterns
in music and train itself

93
00:04:19,019 --> 00:04:21,459
enough to compose a fresh tune.

94
00:04:21,459 --> 00:04:23,380
So here's a question for you.

95
00:04:23,380 --> 00:04:26,920
Which of the following
statements does not hold true?

96
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:30,460
A, activation functions
are threshold functions.

97
00:04:30,460 --> 00:04:34,510
B, error is calculated at each
layer of the neural network.

98
00:04:34,510 --> 00:04:37,320
C, both forward and
back propagation

99
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:40,780
take place during the training
process of a neural network.

100
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:43,890
D, most of the data
processing is carried out

101
00:04:43,890 --> 00:04:45,280
in the hidden layers.

102
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:47,790
Leave your answers in the
comments section below.

103
00:04:47,790 --> 00:04:50,890
Three of you stand a chance
to win Amazon vouchers.

104
00:04:50,890 --> 00:04:52,640
So don't miss it.

105
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:54,660
With deep learning
and neural networks,

106
00:04:54,660 --> 00:04:57,040
we are still taking baby steps.

107
00:04:57,040 --> 00:05:00,190
The growth in this field has
been foreseen by the big names.

108
00:05:00,190 --> 00:05:03,340
Companies such as Google,
Amazon, and NVIDIA

109
00:05:03,340 --> 00:05:06,850
have invested in developing
products such as libraries,

110
00:05:06,850 --> 00:05:09,850
predictive models,
and intuitive GPUs

111
00:05:09,850 --> 00:05:12,710
that support the implementation
of neural networks.

112
00:05:12,710 --> 00:05:14,770
The question dividing
the visionaries

113
00:05:14,770 --> 00:05:17,090
is on the reach of
neural networks--

114
00:05:17,090 --> 00:05:20,160
to what extent can we
replicate the human brain?

115
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:23,050
We'd have to wait a few more
years to give a definite answer,

116
00:05:23,050 --> 00:05:25,330
but if you enjoyed
this video, it

117
00:05:25,330 --> 00:05:27,740
would only take a few
seconds to like and share it.

